'Cause a lot of the times the people

00:08:58.987 --> 00:08:59.970
who get annoyed at this stuff,

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:03.009
aren't the people who
actually watch Trash Taste.

00:09:03.009 --> 00:09:04.327
There's people outside of Trash Taste

00:09:04.327 --> 00:09:07.380
who maybe have some followers
who've watched Trash Taste.

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:09.297
Maybe seen some of the clips
or whatever and they're like,

00:09:09.297 --> 00:09:11.160
"You won't believe what these guys

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:14.490
who I don't already watch
or engage with said."

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:17.320
They don't know how we behave

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:20.450
or how we go towards a
topic or how we tackle it.

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:22.040
It's just like, he just said this thing.

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:23.900
I disagree with it. I'm gonna get angry.

00:09:23.900 --> 00:09:25.690
- What's really weird,

00:09:25.690 --> 00:09:27.807
especially about my
"Jujutsu Kaisen" hot take,

00:09:27.807 --> 00:09:31.900
"hot take", is the fact that
I called "Jujutsu Kaisen" okay

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:33.990
months ago on my own channel.

00:09:33.990 --> 00:09:35.910
No one fucking batted an eye.

00:09:35.910 --> 00:09:38.385
I say it on Trash Taste,
everyone loses their minds.

00:09:38.385 --> 00:09:39.218
- I think 'cause it's Trash Taste, right?

00:09:39.218 --> 00:09:41.050
It's weird, 'cause I feel
we've got to that point now

00:09:41.050 --> 00:09:44.450
where not super small Twitter accounts,

00:09:44.450 --> 00:09:46.810
but some Twitter accounts
with some decent followings

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:50.757
will be like, "This clown
take on Trash Taste XXX."

00:09:50.757 --> 00:09:52.260
But I think that's also kind of cool.

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:54.980
I'm like, "Oh, that's
awesome that people feel like

00:09:54.980 --> 00:09:58.022
we're big enough where they
could just openly criticize us."

00:09:58.022 --> 00:10:00.120
I'm like, "Go ahead, man!"

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:02.820
- It is humbling to think
that my offhand comment

00:10:02.820 --> 00:10:06.010
about an Anime has stirred
up this much controversy.

00:10:06.010 --> 00:10:09.780
I mean, it's kinda cool, but
at the same time, it's like,

00:10:09.780 --> 00:10:12.483
can you not cancel me for
saying that a show is okay?

00:10:12.483 --> 00:10:13.880
I could candidly sleep over it if somebody

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:14.713
gets angry at me on Twitter.

00:10:14.713 --> 00:10:15.672
- Oh, I not sleeping over it.

00:10:15.672 --> 00:10:17.010
I think it's a little like, you know.

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:18.310
- I'm glad.

00:10:18.310 --> 00:10:21.480
Imagine back four or five years ago

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:23.914
if I'd said the same shit,
no one would give a fuck.

00:10:23.914 --> 00:10:24.780
- No one would care.

00:10:24.780 --> 00:10:25.900
- I'm glad that people care!

00:10:25.900 --> 00:10:27.240
Sometimes it's annoying.

00:10:27.240 --> 00:10:29.160
- It's a little too much.
- But I love it.

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:31.911
- Thank you for caring about
my dumb opinion about a show.

00:10:31.911 --> 00:10:33.542
- I don't care about Joey's
opinion, so you shouldn't!

00:10:33.542 --> 00:10:34.750
- I don't even care about my opinion!

00:10:34.750 --> 00:10:35.583
I just said it!

00:10:35.583 --> 00:10:38.700
- Well, I think the argument
is that we are creators

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:41.440
who have a platform and an influence.

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:43.710
I mean, that's why they
call people like us

00:10:43.710 --> 00:10:45.280
influencers, right?
(Joey retching)

00:10:45.280 --> 00:10:46.930
Even though we fucking hate the word.

00:10:46.930 --> 00:10:47.763
- I'm allergic to that word.

00:10:47.763 --> 00:10:48.753
- I love it, actually.

00:10:49.810 --> 00:10:52.330
I've got that evil voice going for me,

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:53.580
so I feel like it works

00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:55.250
when someone calls me
an influencer, you know?

00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:57.143
- It's just the one thing I
don't like about out that word

00:10:57.143 --> 00:11:00.630
is that it can apply to
so many things, you know?

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:03.130
A cult leader is technically
an influencer as well.

00:11:03.130 --> 00:11:04.731
- [Garnt] Those are the OG influencers.

00:11:04.731 --> 00:11:05.690
- They're the OG influencers, right?

00:11:05.690 --> 00:11:07.830
I don't know if I wanna be bunched up

00:11:07.830 --> 00:11:09.670
in those kinds of people.
- I'm kidding, by the way.

00:11:09.670 --> 00:11:10.503
I don't actually like the word.

00:11:10.503 --> 00:11:11.880
I like to think that I make something

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:13.910
that's somewhat entertaining and good.

00:11:13.910 --> 00:11:15.898
- Yeah, I'm just a dude on the internet.

00:11:15.898 --> 00:11:16.870
- [Connor] I don't know, yeah.

00:11:16.870 --> 00:11:18.270
- With a bunch of hot takes.

00:11:20.135 --> 00:11:21.860
- I get it to a certain extent,

00:11:21.860 --> 00:11:24.130
where we do have to be careful about

00:11:24.130 --> 00:11:25.610
some of the stuff we say

00:11:25.610 --> 00:11:27.780
'cause there are some topics that I feel

00:11:27.780 --> 00:11:30.943
we do have to navigate very carefully.

00:11:30.943 --> 00:11:31.776
- [Joey] Of course.

00:11:31.776 --> 00:11:33.740
- Because there are
other creators out there

00:11:33.740 --> 00:11:36.310
who do have a platform, and their words,

00:11:36.310 --> 00:11:39.520
they say shit and their
words have a tangible effect

00:11:39.520 --> 00:11:42.520
on the real world and the
community they talk to,

00:11:42.520 --> 00:11:45.840
but at the same time,
there are some things that

00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:50.720
blows my mind that people
care this much about, right?

00:11:50.720 --> 00:11:54.683
And one of the biggest things
that I don't understand is

00:11:54.683 --> 00:11:59.683
people will take this one
minute, two minute clip

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:02.190
from Trash Taste or
from one of our streams.

00:12:02.190 --> 00:12:04.190
'Cause this happened to me
a bunch of times, right?

00:12:04.190 --> 00:12:06.760
Where I will see this
clip being circulated.

00:12:06.760 --> 00:12:08.650
where it's a one or two minute clip

00:12:08.650 --> 00:12:11.210
from the podcast or my
stream that's not scripted,

00:12:11.210 --> 00:12:14.000
it's just in a conversation
that's most of the time

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:15.540
doesn't even have anything to do

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:17.540
with the take that I'm
saying in that one clip

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:19.400
because it's one or two minutes.

00:12:19.400 --> 00:12:20.480
And they will take this clip

00:12:20.480 --> 00:12:23.737
and then spin it to a whole new level of-

00:12:23.737 --> 00:12:25.600
- I get it, like you've
planned it all out.

00:12:25.600 --> 00:12:26.847
- Yeah!

00:12:26.847 --> 00:12:28.970
- It's a fucking mastermind move.

00:12:28.970 --> 00:12:31.780
- And I think of this in context, right?

00:12:31.780 --> 00:12:35.450
And I'm thinking, I don't
think people who watch our show

00:12:35.450 --> 00:12:37.810
or people who are super fans of the show

00:12:37.810 --> 00:12:40.410
is going to be influenced
by a one minute clip

00:12:40.410 --> 00:12:42.185
of us talking about this one subject

00:12:42.185 --> 00:12:43.540
that most of the time doesn't even

00:12:43.540 --> 00:12:45.640
have to do with the overall conversation,

00:12:45.640 --> 00:12:46.473
it's just most of the time

00:12:46.473 --> 00:12:48.030
just an offhand comment something.

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:50.869
I don't think that's gonna
fucking influence anybody.

00:12:50.869 --> 00:12:52.120
- But on that segment, Joey,

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:53.843
where you spoke about "Jujutsu
Kaisen" and I was like,

00:12:53.843 --> 00:12:56.277
"No, you're a clown. It's good."

00:12:57.340 --> 00:12:58.260
If you're a viewer, it's like,

00:12:58.260 --> 00:13:01.100
how can you argue that you are
being influenced to be like,

00:13:01.100 --> 00:13:03.000
"Jujutsu Kaisen" is mid or okay."

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:05.480
'Cause there's an active argument going on

00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:07.580
where we're saying, "No,
it's not. You're wrong."

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:09.723
So as the viewer, what would
you take away from that?

00:13:09.723 --> 00:13:12.000
It's not, "Oh, I'm gonna think
"Jujutsu Kaisen" is mid."

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:13.040
Even if you're a super fan.

00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:14.460
It's so stupid.

00:13:14.460 --> 00:13:16.110
- But that's what I think I like about

00:13:16.110 --> 00:13:17.570
those kinds of discussions on the show,

00:13:17.570 --> 00:13:20.350
especially when two or all of us

00:13:20.350 --> 00:13:21.783
are arguing against each other, right?

00:13:21.783 --> 00:13:24.570
Is that it gives so many
different points of views,

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:26.850
where it's up to the viewers now

00:13:26.850 --> 00:13:28.557
who you want to agree with, right?

00:13:28.557 --> 00:13:31.467
And it's not so much me saying,

00:13:31.467 --> 00:13:34.640
"Hey, because I think
"Jujutsu Kaisen" is okay,

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:35.970
you should also think that way."

00:13:35.970 --> 00:13:38.450
I mean, if you want to think
that way that's on you, right?

00:13:38.450 --> 00:13:40.750
But it's not like I'm coming out here

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:42.927
fucking starting a demo of being like,

00:13:42.927 --> 00:13:45.147
"Everybody, stand up and rise!

00:13:45.147 --> 00:13:47.103
"Jujutsu Kaisen" is just okay!"

00:13:48.124 --> 00:13:50.650
And start a fucking coup
d'etat over it, right?

00:13:50.650 --> 00:13:52.333
It's like I'm just some fucking-

00:13:53.202 --> 00:13:55.283
Yeah, I just don't get it.

00:13:56.230 --> 00:13:58.530
It's fine to be influenced
by certain things,

00:13:58.530 --> 00:14:03.200
but at the same time, it's
like, it's just a show, bro.

00:14:03.200 --> 00:14:05.270
- I think it's a good
problem to have in our job.

00:14:05.270 --> 00:14:06.103
- Of course

00:14:06.103 --> 00:14:08.970
- People would spend many years

00:14:08.970 --> 00:14:10.570
trying to get to the point where,

00:14:10.570 --> 00:14:12.780
well, we're very fortunate
where people watch Trash Taste

00:14:12.780 --> 00:14:13.800
and people care.

00:14:13.800 --> 00:14:15.380
I feel very lucky that
people wanna get angry

00:14:15.380 --> 00:14:17.305
about small things I joke about.

00:14:17.305 --> 00:14:18.450
- Yeah, that's fine.

00:14:18.450 --> 00:14:20.020
Is it a contention for
cancellation, though?

00:14:20.020 --> 00:14:21.020
Not sure about that.

00:14:22.264 --> 00:14:23.710
- I dunno, it goes back
to my online hate days.

00:14:23.710 --> 00:14:25.690
I've gone to the point now where

00:14:25.690 --> 00:14:29.293
it doesn't really bother me
that much at all, really.

00:14:29.293 --> 00:14:30.147
It's interesting.

00:14:30.147 --> 00:14:33.280
I think this is just 'cause
I've been online for so long now

00:14:33.280 --> 00:14:36.630
where now I'm just kind
of in equilibrium with it.

00:14:36.630 --> 00:14:37.463
I'm like, I don't know.

00:14:37.463 --> 00:14:40.010
- Yeah, I wouldn't even say it's because

00:14:40.010 --> 00:14:43.230
I'm okay with it now or I'm numb to it.

00:14:43.230 --> 00:14:45.940
I think Jessica Nigri said it best.

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:47.757
She said, when someone
asked her about like,

00:14:47.757 --> 00:14:50.300
"How do you deal with internet hate?

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:51.450
How do you get over it?"

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:53.260
And she said like, "You never get over it.

00:14:53.260 --> 00:14:55.982
It still hurts, but you
just learn to live with it."

00:14:55.982 --> 00:14:58.307
- To me, 'cause we have
talked about this a few times,

00:14:58.307 --> 00:15:01.746
but to me, without getting
to the online hate thing,

00:15:01.746 --> 00:15:03.670
the one thing that annoys me

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:06.940
than just people actually
just hating on me

00:15:06.940 --> 00:15:08.840
and hating on my content, for example,

00:15:08.840 --> 00:15:13.147
is just when people are trying
to put words in my mouth.

00:15:13.147 --> 00:15:15.810
To be like, "Garnt said this,

00:15:15.810 --> 00:15:18.600
or Garnt said this and that means X

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:19.760
or that means X, Y, Z."

00:15:19.760 --> 00:15:23.090
And to me, there's nothing that
wants to make me reply more

00:15:23.090 --> 00:15:25.464
than people who are
spreading this idea that-

00:15:25.464 --> 00:15:27.207
- That's the greatest bait of all though.

00:15:27.207 --> 00:15:29.070
- It is, right? It is.

00:15:29.070 --> 00:15:32.600
- Because at that point,
I've seen some instances

00:15:32.600 --> 00:15:34.770
where I say one thing, right?

00:15:34.770 --> 00:15:38.870
And then it just spirals
out into this insane story

00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:41.828
about how I fucking killed
a child or some shit, right?

00:15:41.828 --> 00:15:43.590
(all laughing)

00:15:43.590 --> 00:15:46.040
It's that level of how did you take

00:15:46.040 --> 00:15:47.770
this one little piece of information

00:15:47.770 --> 00:15:49.080
and spin it in a way

00:15:49.080 --> 00:15:50.953
that just couldn't be
further from the truth?

00:15:50.953 --> 00:15:53.653
You are basically writing a
fan fiction at that point.

00:15:54.890 --> 00:15:55.880
And it's like, what?

00:15:55.880 --> 00:15:57.537
And then there are people
who look at that and be like,

00:15:57.537 --> 00:15:59.550
"Oh, yeah. That sounds
like something he'd say."

00:15:59.550 --> 00:16:00.918
I'm like, what?

00:16:00.918 --> 00:16:02.690
- I've been thinking about that a lot.

00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:06.500
- 'Cause I swear to God, I don't
know if the Anime community

00:16:06.500 --> 00:16:08.170
was always like this.

00:16:08.170 --> 00:16:11.610
Because, to me, there are some topics

00:16:11.610 --> 00:16:13.603
that I always used to love
arguing about, you know?

00:16:13.603 --> 00:16:15.273
Because I felt like, to me,

00:16:15.273 --> 00:16:17.720
there's some things where
you really have to be careful

00:16:17.720 --> 00:16:19.960
about what you say in terms of religion,

00:16:19.960 --> 00:16:22.030
politics and stuff like that.

00:16:22.030 --> 00:16:23.630
- Hence the reason why we never
talk about it on the show.

00:16:23.630 --> 00:16:24.970
- We've spoken about a
little bit on Trash Taste.

00:16:24.970 --> 00:16:28.020
- But we try and avoid
it as much as we can.

00:16:28.020 --> 00:16:30.200
- But you know, sometimes
you just want to have

00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:31.500
a fun argument with someone

00:16:31.500 --> 00:16:33.333
where you can just shit on their opinion

00:16:33.333 --> 00:16:35.560
and you don't have to worry about it

00:16:36.420 --> 00:16:38.190
'cause you know that,
at the end of the day,

00:16:38.190 --> 00:16:40.780
the topic doesn't really matter that much.

00:16:40.780 --> 00:16:43.730
And to me, as an Anime fan,

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:45.790
Anime was always one
of those topics for me

00:16:45.790 --> 00:16:47.090
until quite recently.

00:16:47.090 --> 00:16:49.160
And I don't know if
that's just my perception.

00:16:49.160 --> 00:16:51.140
'Cause another topic I would say

00:16:51.140 --> 00:16:54.450
you can easily argue with
anyone about is food.

00:16:54.450 --> 00:16:55.780
Everyone loves arguing about food,

00:16:55.780 --> 00:16:57.680
we do it all of the fucking
time, 'cause it's fun.

00:16:57.680 --> 00:16:59.870
And it's fun because people understand

00:16:59.870 --> 00:17:02.170
that people have different
tastes and opinion, right?

00:17:02.170 --> 00:17:05.650
And to me, Anime was
always at that same level,

00:17:05.650 --> 00:17:08.850
as I can easily argue
about anyone with Anime

00:17:08.850 --> 00:17:12.070
and not have to worry about
hurting their feelings too much

00:17:12.070 --> 00:17:15.040
because I just assume
everyone in our community

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:16.550
has an understanding that,

00:17:16.550 --> 00:17:17.520
Dude, you can have your own taste.

00:17:17.520 --> 00:17:18.353
You can have your own opinion.

00:17:18.353 --> 00:17:19.750
- It's a mutual agreement
that at the end of the day,

00:17:19.750 --> 00:17:21.570
even if this one random internet person

00:17:21.570 --> 00:17:24.230
doesn't think that your
favorite shows as good as it is,

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:26.120
it's like, "Well, that's
not gonna deter me

00:17:26.120 --> 00:17:27.505
from the fact that I still
like this show, right?"

00:17:27.505 --> 00:17:28.338
- It's really just changed

00:17:28.338 --> 00:17:30.893
just 'cause of the scale
of Trash Taste, right?

00:17:32.230 --> 00:17:33.970
There was nothing like
this back in the day.

00:17:33.970 --> 00:17:36.783
Back on "PodTaku", what was
the average viewer count?

00:17:38.930 --> 00:17:42.680
- I think our most viewed
podcast ever was 100K.

00:17:42.680 --> 00:17:44.308
- Which back then was crazy

00:17:44.308 --> 00:17:46.120
for a podcast, that's insane.
- Yeah, it was crazy.

00:17:46.120 --> 00:17:49.150
- Obviously the scale is
completely different now.

00:17:49.150 --> 00:17:53.690
Anime has also been somewhat
more democratized in a way.

00:17:53.690 --> 00:17:54.869
- Democratized.
- It's more readily available.

00:17:54.869 --> 00:17:57.843
- Yeah, it's more
available to more eyes now.

00:17:57.843 --> 00:17:59.643
- It's a lot easier to get ahold of.

00:18:00.820 --> 00:18:02.830
And discourse about it is way more open

00:18:02.830 --> 00:18:03.963
and people are way more
open to talk about it.

00:18:03.963 --> 00:18:06.950
So I think that's some of the reasons why.

00:18:06.950 --> 00:18:09.458
- So the problem is
it's getting to popular.

00:18:09.458 --> 00:18:11.250
(Garnt laughing)
- Well, essentially!

00:18:11.250 --> 00:18:13.510
- You could almost say
it's becoming mainstream.

00:18:13.510 --> 00:18:14.343
- Kinda.

00:18:14.343 --> 00:18:16.237
I always had this image that

00:18:16.237 --> 00:18:19.880
the Anime community felt
like it was about 10,

00:18:19.880 --> 00:18:21.590
five, 10 years behind hat we saw

00:18:21.590 --> 00:18:23.420
with the gaming community, right?

00:18:23.420 --> 00:18:26.210
'Cause it felt like
maybe the gaming industry

00:18:26.210 --> 00:18:28.860
also had this shift where games used to be

00:18:28.860 --> 00:18:31.660
just these fun things you
numb your brain out to,

00:18:31.660 --> 00:18:33.909
it didn't really matter that much.

00:18:33.909 --> 00:18:34.880
You could just have your have fun with it.

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:39.880
And then now games are a big business.

00:18:40.830 --> 00:18:42.310
- It's the same essentially.

00:18:42.310 --> 00:18:45.230
I know that some people gave
"Zelda: Breath of the Wild"

00:18:45.230 --> 00:18:46.690
a seven out of 10 when it came out

00:18:46.690 --> 00:18:48.800
and they got controversy for that,

00:18:48.800 --> 00:18:50.850
'cause they didn't give it
a nine or 10 or something.

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:52.617
- So basically they
got canceled for saying

00:18:52.617 --> 00:18:54.507
"Breath of the Wild" was just okay?

00:18:54.507 --> 00:18:55.720
(Joey and Garnt laughing)

00:18:55.720 --> 00:18:57.125
- No, they said it was just good.

00:18:57.125 --> 00:18:59.807
